# Database and security

- Prefer updating an unapplied migration in place when it has never been applied anywhere; otherwise add a new corrective migration. Do not rewrite applied remote history without approval.
- Do not apply migrations to remote Supabase unless explicitly asked.
- Prefer SECURITY DEFINER helpers with `SET search_path = public` for membership checks to avoid RLS recursion.
- Pick identity fields (`id`, `user_id`, `week_id` / `playoff_round_id`, `submitted_at`) are immutable for all authenticated users, including commissioners. Check immutability before commissioner exceptions. Commissioner authority uses `OLD` week/round ids.
- Players may change only `team_id` on their own picks before `locks_at`; insert/update timestamps are database-controlled.
- Treat `locks_at <= now()` as locked (exact timestamp is locked).
- Keep regular-season and playoff used-team lists separate; serialize reuse checks with namespaced advisory locks.
- `teams` is migration-managed reference data; authenticated app users are read-only.
- Never claim RLS is verified from reading SQL alone — run the database authorization tests when local Supabase is available.
- Do not weaken application-table RLS to make tests pass; grant only the `tests` schema helpers to authenticated.
